# Korenix JetI/O 6520.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Korenix JetI/O 6520 Industrial Intelligent Ethernet I/O Server
# | 
# | Source: JetI/O 6520 User's Manual V0.1 (Jan. 2008)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (Ethernet port 502); FC03 read holding, FC06 write single
# | Module: 4-channel analog output, 16-bit
# | Output ranges (set globally at addr 9):
# | 0 = 0~+10V  (0~10000 = 0~10V)
# | 1 = -10V~+10V  (-10000~10000 = -10V~+10V)
# | 2 = 0~20mA  (0~20000 = 0~20mA)
# | Slew rate (addr 8): 4-bit code per channel packed into one register (ABCD = ch3,ch2,ch1,ch0).
# | Power-on DA values (addr 10-13): stored output value applied on power-up.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Korenix
@model=JetI/O 6520
@description=4-CH analog output Ethernet I/O server, Modbus/TCP. Output range set globally at addr 9 (0=0~+10V, 1=-10V~+10V, 2=0~20mA). Output values at addr 22-25 (s16; 0-10000=0-10V, ±10000=±10V, 0-20000=0-20mA). Slew rate at addr 8 (4-bit code per channel). Power-on values at addr 10-13. Calibration offset/span at addr 14-21.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/korenix-jetio-6520.toml; Source: JetI/O 6520 User's Manual V0.1 (Jan. 2008). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

